{% comment %}
  Markup copied verbatim from the supplied index.html (top bar + site-header).
  Only the hard-coded values are swapped for Shopify objects:
  logo -> settings.logo, nav items -> section.settings.menu, icons -> routes.
{% endcomment %}

<div class="top-bar py-2 bg-drak-crimson-red">
  <div class="container custom-width">
    <div class="row">
      <div class="col-md-4 top-bar__support">
        <a href="{{ section.settings.support_link | default: '#' }}" class="fs14 fw500 text-white">
          {{- section.settings.support_text -}}
        </a>
      </div>
      <div class="col-md-4 top-bar__message text-center fs14 heading-font fw500 text-white">
        {{- section.settings.message -}}
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>
<header class="site-header py-2">
  <div class="container custom-width">
    <nav class="site-header__navbar navbar navbar-expand-xl p-0">
      <a class="site-header__brand navbar-brand" href="{{ routes.root_url }}">
        {%- if settings.logo != blank -%}
          <img
            src="{{ settings.logo | image_url: width: 402 }}"
            alt="{{ settings.logo.alt | default: shop.name | escape }}"
            class="site-header__logo"
          >
        {%- endif -%}
      </a>
      {%- comment -%}
        Below `navbar-expand-xl` the menu is an off-canvas drawer, not a
        collapse. A collapse pushes the page down and leaves the nav competing
        with the hero for the fold; a drawer keeps the header height fixed and
        gives each link a full-width tap target.

        This is Bootstrap's own responsive-offcanvas navbar pattern, so desktop
        is unaffected: at >=1200px `.navbar-expand-xl .offcanvas` is reset to
        `position: static; transform: none; visibility: visible` and the
        `.offcanvas-header` is hidden, leaving the same flex row as before.
      {%- endcomment -%}
      <button
        class="site-header__toggler navbar-toggler"
        type="button"
        data-bs-toggle="offcanvas"
        data-bs-target="#mainNavbar"
        aria-controls="mainNavbar"
        aria-label="{{ 'xd.toggle_navigation' | t }}"
      >
        <span class="navbar-toggler-icon"></span>
      </button>
      <div
        class="site-header__collapse site-header__drawer offcanvas offcanvas-start"
        tabindex="-1"
        id="mainNavbar"
        aria-labelledby="mainNavbarLabel"
      >
        <div class="offcanvas-header site-header__drawer-head">
          {%- comment -%}
            Kept in the DOM but visually hidden: aria-labelledby needs a target
            to name the dialog, while a drawer of nav links does not need a
            visible "Menu" caption.
          {%- endcomment -%}
          <span class="offcanvas-title visually-hidden" id="mainNavbarLabel">
            {{- 'sections.header.menu' | t -}}
          </span>
          <button
            type="button"
            class="btn-close btn-close-white"
            data-bs-dismiss="offcanvas"
            aria-label="{{ 'accessibility.close' | t | default: 'Close' }}"
          ></button>
        </div>
        <div class="offcanvas-body site-header__drawer-body">
          <ul class="site-header__nav navbar-nav mx-auto sm-heading">
            {%- for link in section.settings.menu.links -%}
              <li class="site-header__nav-item nav-item">
                <a
                  class="site-header__nav-link nav-link{% if link.current or link.child_active %} active{% endif %}"
                  href="{{ link.url }}"
                >
                  {{- link.title | escape -}}
                </a>
              </li>
            {%- endfor -%}
          </ul>
          {%- comment -%}
            The top bar's support link is hidden below 768px to keep the sticky
            header short, so it is re-surfaced here rather than lost.
          {%- endcomment -%}
          <div class="site-header__drawer-foot">
            <a
              class="site-header__drawer-account"
              href="{% if customer %}{{ routes.account_url }}{% else %}{{ routes.account_login_url }}{% endif %}"
            >
              <i class="fa-regular fa-user"></i>
              {%- if customer -%}
                {{ 'customer.account.title' | t | default: 'Account' }}
              {%- else -%}
                {{ 'customer.log_in' | t | default: 'Log in' }}
              {%- endif -%}
            </a>
            {%- if section.settings.support_text != blank -%}
              <a class="site-header__drawer-support" href="{{ section.settings.support_link | default: '#' }}">
                {{- section.settings.support_text -}}
              </a>
            {%- endif -%}
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
      {%- comment -%}
        Cart/account sit OUTSIDE .navbar-collapse. In the source build they are
        inside it, which means they vanish on mobile until the burger menu is
        opened (a collapsed .collapse is display:none, so children can't be
        shown by CSS). Desktop layout is unchanged - verified pixel-identical.
      {%- endcomment -%}
      <div class="site-header__ecommoption d-inline-flex flex-row align-items-center gap-4 w-auto">
        {%- comment -%}
          id="cart-icon-bubble" is what Dawn's cart-drawer.js binds to in order
          to open the native drawer and to re-render the item count after an
          AJAX add. Its inner markup must match sections/cart-icon-bubble.liquid.
        {%- endcomment -%}
        <a class="site-header__option site-header__cart" href="{{ routes.cart_url }}" id="cart-icon-bubble">
          {%- render 'xd-cart-icon' -%}
        </a>
        <a
          class="site-header__option site-header__user"
          href="{% if customer %}{{ routes.account_url }}{% else %}{{ routes.account_login_url }}{% endif %}"
        >
          <i class="fa-regular fa-user"></i>
        </a>
      </div>
    </nav>
  </div>
</header>

{% schema %}
{
  "name": "XD Header",
  "settings": [
    {
      "type": "link_list",
      "id": "menu",
      "default": "main-menu",
      "label": "Menu"
    },
    {
      "type": "header",
      "content": "Top bar"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "support_text",
      "label": "Left link text",
      "default": "Customer Support"
    },
    {
      "type": "url",
      "id": "support_link",
      "label": "Left link URL"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "message",
      "label": "Center message",
      "default": "FREE SHIPPING | LIMITED LIFETIME WARRANTY"
    }
  ],
  "enabled_on": {
    "groups": ["header"]
  }
}
{% endschema %}
